<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian 182-day T-bill rate slips.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian 182-day T-bill rate slips.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Lithuanian 182-day T-bills slipped to 10.93 percent at auction on Tuesday from 11.53 percent, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AVG YIELD  LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID    SOLD</p>
<p> 182-day   10.93	11.53     9.40/11.97    50  35.677 33.677</p>
<p>Settlement date for the auction is March 7, and the paper matures on September 5.</p>
<p>The next auction is March 7 when 60 million litas ($15 million) of 91-day paper will be sold and on March 8 when 50 million litas of 91-day paper will sold.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
<p>($ = 3.997 Lithuanian Litas)</p>
</text>
